From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 13:35:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04679/11362] [outer-loop] Log IGE + PoE-World nulls in the ARC
 levers-tried ledger (planner: do not re-propose)

Both operator-directed 2026-06-28 generation levers nulled; record them so the planner
does not re-derive/re-propose them (Failed-Experiment Rerun Discipline).

- Family 1: IGE-style LLM-guided Go-Explore cell selection (arc_ige_cell_selector) ->
  honest_null. Selector exercised with the real LLM; no first-win lift; at submitted
  bins=6 the archive collapses to ~2 cells so selection has nothing to choose among.
  SELECTION over a fixed pool cannot fix GENERATION.
- Family 3: PoE-World weighted product-of-experts CONSENSUS (arc_poe_world_model) ->
  honest_null. The TRUE PoE combination (vs the nulled max-vote exp4749); consensus
  genuinely exercised (8 conflicts, prior swept) but loses to max-vote 0.178 vs 0.558
  in 0/4 games -- ARC is per-cell deterministic, so selecting the best expert beats
  blending. Converges with exp4677/4749: the experts are the ceiling, not the
  combination rule. retire_if_same_verdict gated on consensus_exercised.

Both reinforce the 6-path generation-wall triangulation. Flags default OFF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
